messages:
jess_sales: Heads up — Hyperion (enterprise bank) asked for a POC next week. They want streaming + function/tool calling + structured JSON output mapped to their 'risk_event' schema. Also must meet p95 latency <=250ms for single-token steps, support SSO (SAML), on-prem KMS option, and IP allowlist. Can eng confirm handshake flow, required artifacts (SAML metadata, IPs), and a ballpark pricing estimate for ~500k tokens/day? cc @maria_eng @tom_devex

maria_eng: We can support all that. Quick notes: streaming + tool/function calls are supported by the SDKs. For on-prem KMS we use the Private deployment; BRD: needs vpc peering or an outbound proxy for control plane calls. For p95 250ms we'll likely recommend model + quantization profile and dedicated capacity. What model family are they expecting to run?

jess_sales: They want high-quality answers, leaning toward open Llama-variant. Prefers accuracy over raw cost but CFO wants numbers. They will provide SAML metadata today.

tom_devex: I'll draft a runbook and a minimal demo app. Quick streaming handshake example (JS) we use in POCs — share with them to validate network/handshake requirements:

```js
const ws = new WebSocket('wss://inference.redwood.ai/stream');
ws.onopen = () => {
  ws.send(JSON.stringify({
    type: 'init',
    apikey: process.env.POC_EPHEMERAL_KEY, // short-lived
    tenant: 'hyperion-bank',
    features: ['streaming','tool_calls','struct_output'],
  }));
};
ws.onmessage = (e) => console.log('msg', JSON.parse(e.data));
```

For structured output we recommend embedding a JSON schema example in the init step so the server can validate/annotate. E.g. schema: {"type":"object","properties":{"event_type":{"type":"string"},"score":{"type":"number"}}}

maria_eng: Also important: ephemeral creds + token rotation. For POC we can issue short-lived tokens via our token service; production they should either use short-lived IAM creds or our Private deployment with BYOK. We'll need the IP ranges they allow for WebSocket egress.

rahul_security: From security questionnaire POV: they asked encryption in transit (TLS1.2+), at-rest encryption with KMS or HSM, audit logs, and staff access controls. We can provide SOC2 attestation and a scannable questionnaire. For BYOK we support HSM-managed keys in the Private plan — need legal + contract for key custody. If they require on-prem-only data planes, we can run the control plane in a customer VPC (ent contract).

infra-bot: deploybot: Reserved capacity pool check: us-east-1 has available dedicated nodes next week for a short POC window. Please confirm desired concurrency/throughput so we can reserve.

jess_sales: Concurrency ask: expected peak ~200 qps (short requests), average 50 qps, 500k tokens/day. Demo time requested by Hyperion: next Tue morning PT. Also they want a pricing delta between Hosted vs Dedicated reserved. CFO needs a 30-day estimate.

maria_eng: Ballpark pricing (very rough): Hosted API w/ open model family (quantized) ~ $0.0015 - $0.003 per token depending on model and opt-level, so 500k tokens/day ≈ $750 - $1,500/day. Dedicated reserved (monthly commit) typically reduces unit cost ~40-60% depending on commit level and autoscaling needs — so roughly $300 - $900/day equivalent for committed usage. Final numbers depend on model, batching params, and KV-cache hit rates. I'll prepare two scenarios (hosted vs reserved) and put in the runbook.

tom_devex: I'll assemble the POC checklist and a minimal repo (Rust + Node sample) and a demo manifest. Need: SAML metadata, IP allowlist, preferred model family, sample prompt set for structured output, and their security questionnaire PDF. I'll share the repo link and a one-pager by EOD.

jess_sales: Perfect. Hyperion will send SAML + questionnaire today. Can we also validate their risk schema mapping? They want fields normalized to snake_case and strict types.

maria_eng: Yes — ask them to supply a sample CSV/JSON schema and 20 representative examples. We'll run an eval to ensure structured outputs match with >95% field extraction accuracy. We'll also add a regression test to Redwood Optimize so we can monitor changes during rollout.

rahul_security: I'll take the questionnaire and start filling the security section. If they require penetration testing or dedicated SOC timelines, flag it here.

jess_sales: Thanks team. Demo scheduled tentatively Tue 10:00 PT pending their confirmation. Tom, please drop the runbook link here when ready.

tom_devex: Will do — linking runbook draft: https://redwood.ai/runbooks/hyperion-poc (internal). Also creating a short checklist: [SAML metadata, IP allowlist, sample schema, 20 examples, legal BYOK note].

jess_sales: Awesome — appreciate the quick turn. :thumbsup:
